# Pushizo integration

Apply when the task mentions Pushizo, push notifications, the `@pushizo/*` packages, `pushizo` SDKs or
`api.pushizo.com`.

## Secrets
- Client apps get only the App ID (public). API keys (`hs_live_…`), SDK secrets, webhook secrets (`whsec_…`),
  APNs `.p8` keys and Firebase service accounts stay on the server, in environment variables or a secret manager.
- Never hard-code, log, print or commit them. Add new variables to `.env.example` without values.

## Client SDKs
- Initialize once per app launch (web: in the browser only, never during SSR). Request notification permission after
  a user action. Call `login(externalId)` after sign-in and `logout()` on sign-out.
- Web: `@pushizo/web` or the script `https://api.pushizo.com/sdk-web/PushizoSDK.js`, plus `/PushizoSDKWorker.js` at
  the site root. React/Vue/Angular: `@pushizo/react`, `@pushizo/vue`, `@pushizo/angular`.
- Mobile: iOS SPM `https://github.com/pushizo/pushizo-ios`, Android `com.pushizo:pushizo-android`, Flutter
  `pushizo_flutter`, React Native/Expo `@pushizo/react-native`, Capacitor `@pushizo/capacitor`, Cordova
  `cordova-plugin-pushizo`, MAUI `Pushizo.Maui`, Unity `com.pushizo.unity`.

## Server API
- Use the official SDK: `@pushizo/node`, `pushizo` (PyPI), `pushizo/pushizo-php`, `github.com/pushizo/pushizo-go`,
  `com.pushizo:pushizo-java`, `Pushizo` (NuGet), `pushizo` (RubyGems), `pushizo` (crates.io).
- `POST /v1/notifications` with `target.include_aliases.external_id`, localized `headings`/`contents`, and a
  deterministic `Idempotency-Key` (e.g. `order-1001-shipped`).
- Do not run real sends, schedules or campaign sends unless the user explicitly asks; use
  `target.test_devices_only: true` or `POST /v1/notifications/estimate` during development.
- Errors: `{"error": {"code": "HS_…", "message", "request_id"}}`; honor `Retry-After` on 429; log `request_id`.

## Webhooks
- Verify `Pushizo-Signature: t=…,v1=…` (HMAC-SHA256 of `t + "." + raw body`) on the raw body with the SDK helper,
  tolerance 300 s, constant-time compare; deduplicate by `Pushizo-Event-Id`.

Full guides: https://docs.pushizo.com/docs · Skills with examples: `skills/*/SKILL.md` in
